        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I don't know if this counts as a Jagged Earth wishlist item, or just something to be included in future reprints:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Some Powers (Elemental Boon comes to mind), and some Spirits (Bringer of Dreams and Nightmares, for example) give other Spirits extra Elements for use in meeting elemental threshholds.&nbsp; Particular in complicated games, or when cards/Powers get duplicated, it is difficult to keep track of what additional elements have been given out.&nbsp; The spirit tokens -- being just one color -- didn't really work for that purpose.&nbsp; For my own games, I made a set of element tokens -- just printed out a couple of sets of elements on a piece of cardstock and laminated it -- and found those extremely useful to keep track of which additional elements had been given out and which could not be found on cards/boards.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyway, either as part of the expansion, or just in future printings of the game, this seems like a helpful thing that could be included.&nbsp; Anybody else out there have different ways of keeping track of elements?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
